EXT. CRAB BOAT "SECOND WIND" - MORNING

flat sea. gulls. a thermos steaming on the gunwale.

THE WOMAN, 30s, in a borrowed oilskin two sizes too big, sits on a coil of line holding her phone out over the water like a fishing rod. LEON, 30s, at the wheel, pretends not to watch her. HOODIE GUY, 20s, sits on the hatch cover with his hood up eating a cold sausage roll.

LEON
you wont get signal out there either

THE WOMAN
Worth a try

Her phone BUZZES. She jumps. Looks at the screen. Lifts it.

THE WOMAN (CONT'D)
(into phone)
Hi mum

MUM (V.O.)
(tinny)
Where ARE you. Your dad said you went off with a fisherman

THE WOMAN
Its a boat trip Mum. Its fine.

MUM (V.O.)
Is he nice

THE WOMAN
He's a, hes got a boat

MUM (V.O.)
That's not an answer

Leon turns the wheel half a degree. The boat leans. Hoodie Guy lifts his hood back and looks at her, then at Leon, then at the sausage roll.

HOODIE GUY
She's got her mum on speaker

LEON
Shes not on speaker Leo

THE WOMAN
Its Leo.

LEON
Yeah Leo. He's my nephew. Leo, not Leon. Obviously.

LEO
(shrugging)
Everyone gets it wrong.

MUM (V.O.)
Who's Leo

THE WOMAN
Nobody Mum bye

She ends the call. Silence. The engine thrums.

THE WOMAN (CONT'D)
Im Hannah by the way. You never asked.

LEON
I didnt want to rush it

HANNAH
You rushed the boat

LEON
The boat was an emergency

HANNAH
I was on the pier for ten minutes and you said and I quote get in

LEON
(smiling at the horizon)
And you did.

HANNAH
^
LEO
(simultaneously, mouth full)
Get a room.

Hannah throws a glove at Leo. He catches it. Leon laughs and the boat rolls once, and Hannah steadies herself on his arm. She doesn't take her hand away.

Gulls.
